You know about pet-testing, right? Your pet won't pick up
cursed items, and doesn't even like to move on their
square unless there's food there; if it does move onto
a cursed item (with no food) you'll get a message like
"Idefix moves only reluctantly." Which means you can
tell that items are safe to try on without having to drag
them to the altar. This makes pets really useful even if
you don't need them to fight for you (I've been using
some horses for this in Gehennom). It can be almost
as boring as hauling everything up if you don't have
a leash or whistle, though. (And if you need to get
a new pet, you can usually find a domestic animal
in Sokoban and throw it food, or some versions of
Minetown have guaranteed domestic animals.)

Anyway, you ought to be able to get at least a couple
+1 or +2 armors like that without necessarily
trucking everything to the altar.

